# Security

Loan amount, term, risk band, and the quote are confidential staff lending data. There is no card data, so PCI is not the driver.

The browser calls the BFF only. It never calls the vendor and never sees the vendor URL or `api-key`.

- `VENDOR_API_KEY` and `VENDOR_API_URL` are server env only. Not in React, `VITE_*` vars, git, logs, or error text.
- Do not build the vendor URL from user input.
- Validate on the server even if the form already checked. Use the shared schema (see the TypeScript rule).
- Depend on `pnpm-lock.yaml`.
- BFF CORS stays `http://localhost:5173`.

This foundation has no staff login. Out of scope unless the user asks: SSO, audit log storage, TLS termination, a secret manager, rate limits, and a pen test.

```ts
// Bad
cors({ origin: "*" });

// Good
cors({ origin: "http://localhost:5173" });
```
